#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tg-verdict-poll.py -- deterministic Telegram verdict parser for the archive bot.

Polls getUpdates on the archive bot. Owner-only messages
(chat.id == from.id == TG_CHAT_ID) are parsed line by line for:

    approve <slug> [reason...]
    reject  <slug> [reason...]
    revert  <slug> [reason...]

Each valid verdict line executes the template's curator-approve.sh or
curator-reject.sh with CURATOR_ACTOR=telegram-owner and reason
"telegram verdict[: trailing text]", then replies to the chat with the outcome.

Revert build 2026-08-10: autonomy widened, so the per-item approval gate gave
way to the weekly "what landed on its own" review plus per-card revert. The
revert verb undoes ONE autonomous promotion after the fact:

    - it takes the audited removal path, the template's curator-retire.sh, NOT a
      raw `git revert` of the promotion commit. A promotion commit carries the
      card AND the decisions.log append, so reverting it would erase the audit
      row that records the promotion. curator-retire.sh instead moves the card
      to the lane's rejected/ folder, appends a `retired` verdict with the
      owner's reason, and commits the scoped paths (its git_commit never
      force-pushes).
    - before retiring, the card's current bytes are compared against the blob
      in its landing commit. If it changed since it landed, the revert is
      REFUSED with "changed since it landed": Owner's own edit would go with it,
      so that case needs a human look.
    - same owner-only rule and same per-run cap as approve/reject.

Buttons build 2026-08-04: callback_query updates (the digest's inline
keyboard) are processed too, owner-only, every tap answered via
answerCallbackQuery. Routes:
    aap        -> confirmation message ("Confirm approve all" / "Cancel")
    aapc       -> approve every pending proposal (cap 60 per confirm; a
                  confirmation older than 30 min is refused as expired),
                  actor telegram-owner, reason "telegram button: approve all",
                  consolidated results reply
    aapx       -> cancel (edits the confirmation message)
    rev        -> one compact card per pending proposal (max 15 per tap,
                  oldest first) with Approve/Reject buttons; a held card
                  leads with "⚠ FLAGGED (...)" so the reason is visible
                  before the button
    a:<slug> / r:<slug> -> run the matching gate script, edit the tapped
                  card to the outcome (buttons drop with the edit)
Callback data stays under Telegram's 64-byte cap: slugs longer than 56 chars
ride an index map (keys c1..cN) persisted to
the hub state dir, tg-verdict.cbmap.json.
A bare "approved"/"approve"/"ok"/"yes" message earns a pointer reply and
never runs a gate script.

Taste hold-back build 2026-08-10: the bulk "Approve all" path now holds back
BOTH kinds of flag curator-run persists in proposals/.meta.json — the
injection screen (`screen_flagged`, the source is suspect) and the
deterministic taste veto (`taste_flagged`, the body carries a private-money
figure or a labeled secret value). Both flags demote a proposal to ask-first
precisely so the owner LOOKS at it, and
approve-all is the one path that skips looking. The reply names how many were
held and why. Single verdicts are untouched: `approve <slug>` and the per-card
Approve button still land a flagged proposal, because an explicit single
verdict IS the owner looking.

Contract (build 2026-08-03, buttons 2026-08-04):
  - NO model calls, ever. Stdlib only. Deterministic.
  - Owner-only: any update not from the owner's private chat advances the
    offset silently and is never processed or replied to (non-owner button
    taps are answered -- spinner cleared -- but never acted on).
  - Never crashes: pre-processing failures (network, bad JSON) log to
    the hub state dir verdict-poll.log and exit 0 with the offset preserved for
    retry. Per-message failures log, and the offset ALWAYS advances past a
    message once processing was attempted (a poison message cannot wedge
    the loop). The offset file is written atomically after every message.
  - Concurrency: flock on tg-verdict.lock; an overlapping run exits instantly.
  - Per-run cap: 20 gate-script executions for text verdicts and single-card
    buttons. "Approve all" has its own cap of 60 per confirmed tap. Unstarted
    messages wait for the next run (offset not advanced); excess verdicts
    inside one message get a FAILED-resend reply.
  - Packet-level phrases ("approve as recommended", "reject the packet",
    "approve all/everything") never run a gate script: one pointer reply
    (Claude executes those), offset advances normally. Slug "as" is reserved.
  - Files touched: <state>/hub/tg-verdict.{offset,lock,cbmap.json}
    and <state>/hub/verdict-poll.log. Nothing else (the gate scripts own
    their own writes).

Sovereign transition build 2026-09-11: routine archive decisions moved into
the Sovereign app (Review). Every approve/reject route above, typed or
button, historical or new, now answers with a pointer to Sovereign and runs
NO gate script; "Review cards" reports the count and sends no buttons.
`revert` is the one verdict still executed here (audited retire path).
Owner filtering, callback acknowledgement, offset and lock are unchanged.

Run every 60s by launchd job com.sov.cron.tg-verdict-poll via cron-run-hub.sh.
Self-test (no network; only writes are throwaway tempfiles for the cbmap
round-trip): tg-verdict-poll.py --self-test
"""

import fcntl
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import traceback
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
STATE_DIR = os.path.join(os.environ.get("SOV_STATE_DIR") or os.path.join(HOME, ".local", "state", "sovereign"), "hub")
TEMPLATE_BIN = os.path.join(os.environ.get("SOV_TEMPLATE") or os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))), "bin")
OFFSET_FILE = os.path.join(STATE_DIR, "tg-verdict.offset")
LOCK_FILE = os.path.join(STATE_DIR, "tg-verdict.lock")
CBMAP_FILE = os.path.join(STATE_DIR, "tg-verdict.cbmap.json")
LOG_FILE = os.path.join(STATE_DIR, "verdict-poll.log")
ENV_FILE = os.environ.get(
    "TG_ENV_FILE", os.path.join(HOME, ".config", "sovereign", "telegram.env")
)
GATE = {
    "approve": os.path.join(TEMPLATE_BIN, "curator-approve.sh"),
    "reject": os.path.join(TEMPLATE_BIN, "curator-reject.sh"),
}
# The audited removal path for a trusted card. Deliberately NOT in GATE: revert
# has a pre-check (unchanged-since-landing) that approve/reject do not.
RETIRE = os.path.join(TEMPLATE_BIN, "curator-retire.sh")


def _read_pointer(path, default):
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            return f.read().strip() or default
    except OSError:
        return default


# The curator lane (same pointer-file fallbacks _curator-lib.sh uses).
VAULT = _read_pointer(
    os.path.join(HOME, ".brain-root"),
    os.environ.get("SOVS_VAULT", ""),
)
LANE_NAME = _read_pointer(os.path.join(HOME, ".curator-lane"), "archivist")
LANE_DIR = os.path.join(VAULT, "raw", "workspaces", LANE_NAME)
PROPOSALS_DIR = os.path.join(LANE_DIR, "proposals")
INBOX_FILE = os.path.join(LANE_DIR, "INBOX.md")
META_FILE = os.path.join(PROPOSALS_DIR, ".meta.json")
KNOWLEDGE_DIR = os.path.join(VAULT, "knowledge")
KNOWLEDGE_SUBS = ("entities", "concepts", "syntheses")

# Verb case-insensitive; slug strictly lowercase kebab.
VERDICT_RE = re.compile(
    r"^((?i:approve|reject|revert))\s+([a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*)\s*(.*)$"
)

# Bulk-approve hold-back (see hold_flags). A digest line carries zero or more
# flag marks between the "(type, conf, tag)" head and the " — reason":
#   - **slug** (entity, high, new) ⚠ SCREENED ⚠ TASTE — why it matters
# Fallback only; proposals/.meta.json is the real source of both flags.
INBOX_FLAG_RE = re.compile(r"^- \*\*([^*]+)\*\* \([^)]*\)((?: ⚠ (?:SCREENED|TASTE))+)")
SCREEN_LABEL = "injection screen"

# Packet-level phrases ("approve as recommended", "reject the packet", ...)
# are verdicts on a whole review packet, executed by Claude (the relay),
# never by this bot. Detected on the whole message BEFORE per-line parsing.
PACKET_PHRASE_RE = re.compile(
    r"^(approve|reject)\s+(as\s+recommended|the\s+packet|all|everything)\b",
    re.IGNORECASE,
)
# Slugs that can never name a proposal (guards "approve as ..." misparses).
# "all"/"everything" are reserved so a sweeping phrase can never be read as a
# single-card verdict. PACKET_PHRASE_RE already catches "approve all" and
# "reject all" at the whole-message level; "revert all" has no packet meaning
# at all, and must never resolve to a card literally named "all".
RESERVED_SLUGS = frozenset(["as", "all", "everything"])
# Sovereign transition (2026-09-11): routine archive decisions moved into the
# Sovereign app. This channel notifies; every approve/reject route below
# answers with this pointer and runs NO gate script. `revert` stays live on
# purpose: it is the audited undo for act-and-report landings (the Sunday
# landed-review tells the owner to use it) and Sovereign has no revert yet.
SOVEREIGN_REPLY = (
    "Decisions moved to Sovereign. Open Sovereign \u2192 Review to compare and "
    "decide. This channel only notifies now; revert <slug> still works here."
)
PACKET_REPLY = SOVEREIGN_REPLY

# A bare acknowledgment is not a verdict: point at the buttons instead.
BARE_ACK_RE = re.compile(r"^(approved|approve|ok|yes)[.!]*$", re.IGNORECASE)
BARE_REPLY = SOVEREIGN_REPLY

POLL_TIMEOUT = 5        # Telegram long-poll seconds
HTTP_TIMEOUT = 25       # socket timeout; must exceed POLL_TIMEOUT
MAX_VERDICTS = 20       # gate executions per run (text + single-card buttons)
MAX_APPROVE_ALL = 60    # gate executions per confirmed approve-all tap
STALE_CONFIRM_SECS = 1800   # a confirm older than this is refused
GATE_TIMEOUT = 180      # seconds per gate script (does a git commit + push)
CB_SLUG_MAX = 56        # longest slug sent literally in callback_data
USAGE = (
    "usage: revert <slug> [reason], one per line, slug lowercase kebab-case. "
    "Approve and reject moved to Sovereign \u2192 Review."
)
EXPIRED_CARD_REPLY = SOVEREIGN_REPLY


def log(msg):
    try:
        with open(LOG_FILE, "a") as f:
            f.write(
                "%s tg-verdict-poll %s\n"
                % (time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z"), msg)
            )
    except OSError:
        pass


def load_env():
    conf = {}
    with open(ENV_FILE) as f:
        for line in f:
            line = line.strip()
            if not line or line.startswith("#") or "=" not in line:
                continue
            k, _, v = line.partition("=")
            conf[k.strip()] = v.strip().strip('"').strip("'")
    return conf


def api(token, method, params):
    data = urllib.parse.urlencode(params).encode()
    req = urllib.request.Request(
        "https://api.telegram.org/bot%s/%s" % (token, method), data=data
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=HTTP_TIMEOUT) as resp:
        return json.load(resp)


def read_offset():
    try:
        with open(OFFSET_FILE) as f:
            return int(f.read().strip())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def write_offset(value):
    tmp = OFFSET_FILE + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        f.write("%d\n" % value)
        f.flush()
        os.fsync(f.fileno())
    os.replace(tmp, OFFSET_FILE)


def html_escape(s):
    """Escape &, <, > for Telegram parse_mode=HTML (order matters: & first)."""
    return (s or "").replace("&", "&amp;").replace("<", "&lt;").replace(">", "&gt;")


def is_packet_phrase(text):
    """True when the whole message is a packet-level verdict for Claude
    (the relay), e.g. 'approve as recommended' -- never for this bot."""
    return bool(PACKET_PHRASE_RE.match((text or "").strip()))


def is_bare_ack(text):
    """True when the whole message is a bare 'approved'/'approve'/'ok'/'yes'
    (optionally punctuated) -- pointed at the buttons, never a gate run."""
    return bool(BARE_ACK_RE.match((text or "").strip()))


def parse_verdicts(text):
    """Return (verdicts, starts_with_verb).

    verdicts: list of (verb, slug, trailing) from valid lines. Lines whose
    slug is reserved (e.g. 'as', 'all') never parse as verdicts.
    starts_with_verb: message text starts with approve/reject/revert (any
    case), used to decide whether an invalid message earns one usage reply.
    """
    verdicts = []
    for raw in (text or "").splitlines():
        m = VERDICT_RE.match(raw.strip())
        if m and m.group(2) not in RESERVED_SLUGS:
            verdicts.append((m.group(1).lower(), m.group(2), m.group(3).strip()))
    lead = (text or "").strip().lower()
    starts = lead.startswith(("approve", "reject", "revert"))
    return verdicts, starts


def owner_message(update, chat_id):
    """Return the message dict if this update is a text message from the
    owner's private chat (chat.id == from.id == TG_CHAT_ID), else None."""
    msg = update.get("message")
    if not isinstance(msg, dict):
        return None
    chat = msg.get("chat") or {}
    frm = msg.get("from") or {}
    if str(chat.get("id")) != chat_id or str(frm.get("id")) != chat_id:
        return None
    if not isinstance(msg.get("text"), str):
        return None
    return msg


def owner_callback(update, chat_id):
    """Return the callback_query dict if it is from the owner (from.id ==
    TG_CHAT_ID) with string callback data, else None."""
    cb = update.get("callback_query")
    if not isinstance(cb, dict):
        return None
    frm = cb.get("from") or {}
    if str(frm.get("id")) != chat_id:
        return None
    if not isinstance(cb.get("data"), str):
        return None
    return cb


def route_callback(data):
    """Pure routing table for callback data. Returns (route, arg):
    ('aap'|'aapc'|'aapx'|'rev', None), ('approve'|'reject', token),
    or (None, None) for anything unknown."""
    if data == "aap":
        return ("aap", None)
    if data == "aapc":
        return ("aapc", None)
    if data == "aapx":
        return ("aapx", None)
    if data == "rev":
        return ("rev", None)
    if isinstance(data, str) and data.startswith("a:") and len(data) > 2:
        return ("approve", data[2:])
    if isinstance(data, str) and data.startswith("r:") and len(data) > 2:
        return ("reject", data[2:])
    return (None, None)


def cbmap_load(path=None):
    """Load the callback index map (token -> slug); {} on any problem."""
    try:
        with open(path or CBMAP_FILE) as f:
            data = json.load(f)
        if isinstance(data, dict):
            return {str(k): str(v) for k, v in data.items()}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        pass
    return {}


def cbmap_save(mapping, path=None):
    """Atomically persist the callback index map."""
    path = path or CBMAP_FILE
    tmp = path + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(mapping, f)
        f.flush()
        os.fsync(f.fileno())
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def cb_token(slug, cbmap):
    """Callback-data token for a slug. The slug itself when it fits under
    Telegram's 64-byte callback_data cap ('a:'/'r:' prefix + <=56 chars);
    otherwise a short index key c1..cN. Returns (token, new_cbmap)."""
    if len(slug) <= CB_SLUG_MAX:
        return slug, cbmap
    for k, v in cbmap.items():
        if v == slug:
            return k, cbmap
    n = 1
    while "c%d" % n in cbmap:
        n += 1
    out = dict(cbmap)
    out["c%d" % n] = slug
    return "c%d" % n, out


def resolve_slug(arg, cbmap, pending):
    """Resolve a callback token to a slug. Literal pending slugs win; c<N>
    tokens go through the map (None when the map has rotated = stale button);
    anything else passes through for the gate script to refuse loudly."""
    if arg in pending:
        return arg
    if re.match(r"^c\d+$", arg or ""):
        return cbmap.get(arg)
    return arg


def pending_slugs():
    """Slugs of the proposals on disk, oldest first (mtime, then name)."""
    try:
        names = os.listdir(PROPOSALS_DIR)
    except OSError:
        return []
    entries = []
    for name in names:
        if name.startswith(".") or not name.endswith(".md"):
            continue
        path = os.path.join(PROPOSALS_DIR, name)
        try:
            entries.append((os.path.getmtime(path), name[:-3]))
        except OSError:
            continue
    entries.sort()
    return [slug for _, slug in entries]


def taste_label(reason):
    """'taste: <what fired>' from curator-run's taste_reason, which reads
    "taste veto: evm wallet address" (or "..., email address x2"). The reason
    names the RULES that fired and deliberately never echoes the matched text,
    so it is safe to put in a Telegram reply. Detail-free flag -> plain label."""
    r = re.sub(r"^\s*taste veto:\s*", "", (reason or "").strip(), flags=re.I)
    return "taste: " + r if r else "taste veto"


def hold_flags():
    """{slug: why} for every pending proposal a BULK approve must not sweep.

    Two independent demotions, one consequence. The injection screen
    (`screen_flagged`) says the SOURCE is suspect; the deterministic taste veto
    (`taste_flagged`) says the BODY carries a private-money figure or a labeled
    secret value. Both demote to ask-first for the same reason: the owner is
    supposed to LOOK. Approve-all is the one path that skips looking, so both are
    held back from it (basis: kyambogo landed 27s after its SCREENED digest,
    2026-08-09; taste added 2026-08-10).

    Wallets, vendor-prefixed keys and contact details are NOT in this list any
    more. Since 2026-08-20 curator-run redacts those out of the card in place
    (there is no decision in them for the owner to make) and never sets
    taste_flagged for them, so they no longer hold anything back from a bulk
    approve. That is the whole point of the change: the queue drains.

    Reads proposals/.meta.json (curator-run persists both flags plus
    taste_reason there); falls back to the current INBOX digest's "⚠ SCREENED"
    and "⚠ TASTE" marks for proposals judged before those fields existed.
    Unreadable state -> nothing held, exactly the pre-flag behavior."""
    screened, tasted = set(), {}
    try:
        with open(META_FILE) as f:
            meta = json.load(f)
        for slug, entry in meta.items():
            if not isinstance(entry, dict):
                continue
            if entry.get("screen_flagged"):
                screened.add(slug)
            if entry.get("taste_flagged"):
                tasted[slug] = entry.get("taste_reason") or ""
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        pass
    try:
        with open(INBOX_FILE) as f:
            for line in f:
                m = INBOX_FLAG_RE.match(line)
                if not m:
                    continue
                slug, marks = m.group(1).strip(), m.group(2)
                if "SCREENED" in marks:
                    screened.add(slug)
                if "TASTE" in marks and slug not in tasted:
                    tasted[slug] = ""  # digest carries the mark, not the reason
    except OSError:
        pass
    flags = {slug: SCREEN_LABEL for slug in screened}
    for slug, reason in tasted.items():
        label = taste_label(reason)
        flags[slug] = flags[slug] + " + " + label if slug in flags else label
    return flags


def split_screened(slugs, flags=None):
    """(clean, held) — held are the proposals hold_flags() withholds from a
    bulk approve, in the order they arrived. Pass `flags` to reuse one read."""
    if flags is None:
        flags = hold_flags()
    clean = [s for s in slugs if s not in flags]
    held = [s for s in slugs if s in flags]
    return clean, held


def held_summary(held, flags):
    """One line naming how many were held and why, for a bulk-approve reply:
    "held 2 (1 injection screen, 1 taste: evm wallet address) — ..." """
    if not held:
        return ""
    counts, order = {}, []
    for slug in held:
        why = flags.get(slug) or "flagged"
        if why not in counts:
            order.append(why)
        counts[why] = counts.get(why, 0) + 1
    return "held %d (%s) — review with the Review cards button or approve by slug" % (
        len(held),
        ", ".join("%d %s" % (counts[w], w) for w in order),
    )


def held_lines(held, flags):
    """Reply lines for what a bulk approve held back: the summary line, then
    one line per proposal carrying the verdict that releases it. Holding back
    is only about the BULK path — an explicit `approve <slug>` (or the per-card
    Approve button) IS the owner looking, and stays permitted."""
    if not held:
        return []
    lines = [held_summary(held, flags)]
    for slug in held:
        lines.append(
            "HELD %s: %s — read it, then: approve %s"
            % (slug, flags.get(slug) or "flagged", slug)
        )
    return lines


def card_text(slug, flags=None):
    """Message text for one review card. A held proposal LEADS with why it is
    held, so the owner sees the flag before the Approve button, not after."""
    typ, conf, reason = proposal_info(slug)
    why = (flags or {}).get(slug)
    head = "⚠ FLAGGED (%s)\n" % html_escape(why) if why else ""
    return "%s<b>%s</b> (%s, %s)\n%s" % (
        head,
        html_escape(slug),
        html_escape(typ),
        html_escape(conf),
        html_escape(reason),
    )


def proposal_info(slug):
    """(type, confidence, one-line reason) for a pending proposal, best
    effort from the note frontmatter, proposals/.meta.json, and INBOX.md."""
    typ, conf, reason = "?", "?", ""
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(PROPOSALS_DIR, slug + ".md")) as f:
            head = f.read(4000)
        m = re.search(r"^---\n(.*?)^---", head, re.S | re.M)
        if m:
            t = re.search(r"^type:\s*(\S+)", m.group(1), re.M)
            if t:
                typ = t.group(1)
    except OSError:
        pass
    try:
        with open(META_FILE) as f:
            meta = json.load(f)
        conf = (meta.get(slug) or {}).get("confidence") or conf
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        pass
    try:
        with open(INBOX_FILE) as f:
            inbox = f.read()
        m = re.search(
            r"^- \*\*%s\*\* \(([^)]*)\) — (.*)$" % re.escape(slug),
            inbox,
            re.M,
        )
        if m:
            parts = [p.strip() for p in m.group(1).split(",")]
            if parts and parts[0]:
                typ = parts[0]
            if len(parts) > 1 and conf == "?":
                conf = parts[1]
            reason = m.group(2).strip()
    except OSError:
        pass
    if not reason:
        reason = "(pending from an earlier run)"
    return typ, conf, reason


def first_error_line(*streams):
    """Best error line from gate output. Gate scripts print a status line
    first ("approving x.md"), so the first non-empty line is usually NOT the
    failure. Prefer the first line containing REFUSED or error
    (case-insensitive); otherwise fall back to the LAST non-empty line."""
    fallback = ""
    for s in streams:
        for line in (s or "").splitlines():
            line = line.strip()
            if not line:
                continue
            low = line.lower()
            if "refused" in low or "error" in low:
                return line
            fallback = line
    return fallback


def run_gate(verb, slug, reason):
    """Execute the gate script for one verdict. Returns the reply line."""
    env = dict(os.environ)
    env["CURATOR_ACTOR"] = "telegram-owner"
    try:
        cp = subprocess.run(
            [GATE[verb], slug, reason],
            capture_output=True,
            text=True,
            timeout=GATE_TIMEOUT,
            env=env,
        )
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        log("verdict %s %s TIMEOUT after %ds" % (verb, slug, GATE_TIMEOUT))
        return "FAILED %s: gate script timed out" % slug
    except OSError as e:
        log("verdict %s %s exec error: %s" % (verb, slug, e))
        return "FAILED %s: %s" % (slug, e)
    log("verdict %s %s rc=%d reason=%r" % (verb, slug, cp.returncode, reason))
    if cp.returncode == 0:
        return ("landed: %s" if verb == "approve" else "rejected: %s") % slug
    err = first_error_line(cp.stdout, cp.stderr) or ("exit %d" % cp.returncode)
    return "FAILED %s: %s" % (slug, err)


def knowledge_paths(slug):
    """Every trusted card matching a slug, vault-relative. Normally 0 or 1;
    2+ means the same slug exists in two knowledge folders, which is ambiguous
    and must never be resolved by guessing."""
    found = []
    for sub in KNOWLEDGE_SUBS:
        rel = "knowledge/%s/%s.md" % (sub, slug)
        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(VAULT, rel)):
            found.append(rel)
    return found


def git_out(*args):
    """Run git in the vault. Returns (rc, stdout, stderr) with text stdout."""
    try:
        cp = subprocess.run(
            ["git", "-C", VAULT] + list(args),
            capture_output=True,
            timeout=60,
        )
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        return (1, b"", str(e).encode())
    return (cp.returncode, cp.stdout, cp.stderr)


def landing_commit(relpath):
    """Short hash of the commit that landed `relpath` in knowledge/.

    The newest `curator: approve <relpath>` commit touching the path, so an
    update landing resolves to the update rather than the original add.
    Falls back to the first-add commit, then "".
    """
    rc, out, _ = git_out(
        "log", "--format=%h\x1f%s", "--max-count=200", "--", relpath
    )
    if rc == 0:
        for line in out.decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines():
            if "\x1f" not in line:
                continue
            h, subject = line.split("\x1f", 1)
            if subject.strip() == "curator: approve %s" % relpath:
                return h.strip()
    rc, out, _ = git_out(
        "log", "-1", "--format=%h", "--diff-filter=A", "--", relpath
    )
    return out.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip() if rc == 0 else ""


def changed_since_landing(relpath, commit):
    """True when the card on disk differs from its bytes in `commit`.

    Compared as raw bytes: a reverted card must be exactly what the curator
    landed, otherwise the owner's own later edit would be carried out with it.
    """
    rc, blob, _ = git_out("show", "%s:%s" % (commit, relpath))
    if rc != 0:
        return True  # cannot prove it is unchanged, so refuse
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(VAULT, relpath), "rb") as f:
            return f.read() != blob
    except OSError:
        return True


def run_revert(slug, reason):
    """Undo one landed promotion. Returns the reply line.

    Audited path: curator-retire.sh (moves the card to the lane's rejected/
    archive, logs a `retired` verdict, commits scoped paths, plain push). A raw
    `git revert` of the promotion commit is deliberately NOT used: that commit
    also carries the decisions.log append, so reverting it would erase the row
    recording the promotion.
    """
    found = knowledge_paths(slug)
    if not found:
        log("revert %s: no trusted card" % slug)
        return "FAILED %s: no trusted card by that name in knowledge/" % slug
    if len(found) > 1:
        log("revert %s: ambiguous (%s)" % (slug, ", ".join(found)))
        return "FAILED %s: ambiguous, that slug exists in %d knowledge folders" % (
            slug,
            len(found),
        )
    relpath = found[0]

    commit = landing_commit(relpath)
    if not commit:
        log("revert %s: no landing commit for %s" % (slug, relpath))
        return (
            "FAILED %s: cannot find the commit that landed it, needs a manual look"
            % slug
        )
    if changed_since_landing(relpath, commit):
        log("revert %s: changed since landing commit %s, refused" % (slug, commit))
        return (
            "FAILED %s: changed since it landed (commit %s). Reverting would take "
            "the later edit with it, so this one needs a manual look." % (slug, commit)
        )

    env = dict(os.environ)
    env["CURATOR_ACTOR"] = "telegram-owner"
    try:
        cp = subprocess.run(
            [RETIRE, slug, reason],
            capture_output=True,
            text=True,
            timeout=GATE_TIMEOUT,
            env=env,
        )
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        log("revert %s TIMEOUT after %ds" % (slug, GATE_TIMEOUT))
        return "FAILED %s: retire script timed out" % slug
    except OSError as e:
        log("revert %s exec error: %s" % (slug, e))
        return "FAILED %s: %s" % (slug, e)
    log("revert %s rc=%d commit=%s reason=%r" % (slug, cp.returncode, commit, reason))
    if cp.returncode == 0:
        return "reverted: %s (was %s, now in rejected/)" % (slug, commit)
    err = first_error_line(cp.stdout, cp.stderr) or ("exit %d" % cp.returncode)
    return "FAILED %s: %s" % (slug, err)


def run_verdict(verb, slug, trailing):
    """Dispatch one parsed verdict line to its executor."""
    if verb == "revert":
        reason = "telegram revert" + (": " + trailing if trailing else "")
        return run_revert(slug, reason)
    reason = "telegram verdict" + (": " + trailing if trailing else "")
    return run_gate(verb, slug, reason)


def send_reply(token, chat_id, text, reply_markup=None, parse_mode=None):
    try:
        if len(text) > 3900:
            text = text[:3900] + "\n...[truncated]"
        params = {"chat_id": chat_id, "text": text}
        if reply_markup is not None:
            params["reply_markup"] = json.dumps(reply_markup)
        if parse_mode:
            params["parse_mode"] = parse_mode
        r = api(token, "sendMessage", params)
        if not r.get("ok"):
            log("reply not ok: %s" % r.get("description", "?"))
    except Exception as e:
        log("reply send failed: %s" % e)


def answer_callback(token, cb_id, text=None):
    """Always answer a callback query so the tap spinner clears."""
    try:
        params = {"callback_query_id": cb_id}
        if text:
            params["text"] = text
        r = api(token, "answerCallbackQuery", params)
        if not r.get("ok"):
            log("answerCallbackQuery not ok: %s" % r.get("description", "?"))
    except Exception as e:
        log("answerCallbackQuery failed: %s" % e)


def edit_message(token, chat_id, message_id, text):
    """Edit a bot message in place. reply_markup is omitted on purpose:
    the edit drops the tapped message's buttons."""
    try:
        r = api(
            token,
            "editMessageText",
            {"chat_id": chat_id, "message_id": message_id, "text": text},
        )
        if not r.get("ok"):
            log("editMessageText not ok: %s" % r.get("description", "?"))
    except Exception as e:
        log("editMessageText failed: %s" % e)


def edit_or_reply(token, chat_id, message_id, text):
    if message_id:
        edit_message(token, chat_id, message_id, text)
    else:
        send_reply(token, chat_id, text)


def handle_callback(cb, token, chat_id, budget):
    """Process one owner callback tap. The query is already answered.
    Returns the number of gate executions used (always 0 since the
    Sovereign transition: no button decides anything any more).

    Historical buttons keep getting a clear answer: a tap on an old digest's
    "Approve all" or on an old card's Approve/Reject edits that message to
    the pointer, so the buttons drop and nothing lands. "Review cards" no
    longer sends cards with buttons; it reports the count and points at the
    app. Cancel still cancels. Owner filtering happened in handle_update.
    """
    data = cb.get("data") or ""
    route, arg = route_callback(data)
    msg = cb.get("message") or {}
    msg_id = msg.get("message_id")

    if route in ("aap", "aapc", "approve", "reject"):
        log("callback %s: refused, decisions live in Sovereign (no gate run)" % route)
        edit_or_reply(token, chat_id, msg_id, SOVEREIGN_REPLY)
        return 0

    if route == "aapx":
        log("callback aapx: cancelled")
        edit_or_reply(token, chat_id, msg_id, "Cancelled.")
        return 0

    if route == "rev":
        n = len(pending_slugs())
        log("callback rev: %d pending, pointing at Sovereign (no cards sent)" % n)
        if not n:
            send_reply(token, chat_id, "Nothing pending.")
            return 0
        send_reply(
            token,
            chat_id,
            "%d proposal%s waiting. %s" % (n, "" if n == 1 else "s", SOVEREIGN_REPLY),
        )
        return 0

    log("callback unknown data %r ignored" % data)
    return 0


def handle_update(update, token, chat_id, budget):
    """Process one update (message or button tap). Returns gate executions used."""
    raw_cb = update.get("callback_query")
    if isinstance(raw_cb, dict):
        # Always answer, owner or not, so the client's tap spinner clears.
        answer_callback(token, raw_cb.get("id", ""))
        cb = owner_callback(update, chat_id)
        if cb is None:
            log(
                "callback ignored (non-owner or malformed) update=%s"
                % update.get("update_id")
            )
            return 0
        return handle_callback(cb, token, chat_id, budget)
    msg = owner_message(update, chat_id)
    if msg is None:
        return 0  # silent: not the owner, or not a text message
    if is_bare_ack(msg["text"]):
        send_reply(token, chat_id, BARE_REPLY)
        return 0  # a bare "approved"/"ok"/"yes" never runs a gate script
    if is_packet_phrase(msg["text"]):
        send_reply(token, chat_id, PACKET_REPLY)
        return 0  # no gate scripts; offset advances normally in poll()
    verdicts, starts = parse_verdicts(msg["text"])
    if not verdicts:
        if starts:
            send_reply(token, chat_id, USAGE)
        return 0
    used = 0
    replies = []
    pointed = False
    for verb, slug, trailing in verdicts:
        if verb in ("approve", "reject"):
            # Sovereign transition: typed verdicts no longer run a gate script.
            log("verdict %s %s refused, decisions live in Sovereign" % (verb, slug))
            if not pointed:
                replies.append(SOVEREIGN_REPLY)
                pointed = True
            continue
        if used >= budget:
            replies.append(
                "FAILED %s: per-run cap (%d) reached, resend this verdict"
                % (slug, MAX_VERDICTS)
            )
            continue
        replies.append(run_verdict(verb, slug, trailing))
        used += 1
    send_reply(token, chat_id, "\n".join(replies))
    return used


def poll():
    os.makedirs(STATE_DIR, exist_ok=True)

    # Concurrency guard: overlapping runs exit instantly.
    lock_fd = os.open(LOCK_FILE, os.O_CREAT | os.O_RDWR, 0o600)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(lock_fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError:
        print("lock held by another run, exiting")
        return 0

    conf = load_env()
    token = conf.get("TG_BOT_TOKEN", "")
    chat_id = conf.get("TG_CHAT_ID", "")
    if not token or not chat_id:
        log("ERROR TG_BOT_TOKEN/TG_CHAT_ID unset in %s" % ENV_FILE)
        print("env incomplete, exiting")
        return 0

    offset = read_offset()
    if offset is None:
        write_offset(0)
        offset = 0

    params = {
        "timeout": POLL_TIMEOUT,
        "limit": 100,
        "allowed_updates": json.dumps(["message", "callback_query"]),
    }
    if offset > 0:
        params["offset"] = offset

    # Failures up to here (and in getUpdates itself) preserve the offset:
    # the top-level handler logs them and the next run retries.
    resp = api(token, "getUpdates", params)
    if not resp.get("ok"):
        log("getUpdates not ok: %s" % resp.get("description", "?"))
        print("getUpdates not ok")
        return 0

    updates = sorted(resp.get("result", []), key=lambda u: u.get("update_id", 0))
    verdicts_run = 0
    processed = 0
    for u in updates:
        if verdicts_run >= MAX_VERDICTS:
            break  # unstarted messages wait for the next run, offset untouched
        try:
            verdicts_run += handle_update(u, token, chat_id, MAX_VERDICTS - verdicts_run)
        except Exception:
            log(
                "update %s handler error: %s"
                % (
                    u.get("update_id"),
                    traceback.format_exc().strip().splitlines()[-1],
                )
            )
        # Poison rule: once processing was attempted, ALWAYS advance.
        write_offset(u["update_id"] + 1)
        processed += 1
    print(
        "updates=%d processed=%d verdicts=%d offset=%s"
        % (len(updates), processed, verdicts_run, read_offset())
    )
    return 0


